The two-proportion z-test for comparing proportions p₁ and p₂ uses the pooled proportion p̂ = (x₁+x₂)/(n₁+n₂) for the standard error under H₀. This is standard — the implementation correctly uses the **overall** pooled rate (which includes the candidate site) for the SE calculation, while the **numerator** is `otherSitesFinalYield - siteFinalYield`. This is the standard Pearson chi-squared/z-test formulation.

